@page "/projects/blazor-app/data"
@page "/projects/game-development/versus-with-verses"

<div class="project-page page-content">
	<header class="project-header">
		<p class="eyebrow">Game Development</p>
		<h1>Versus With Verses</h1>
		<p class="tagline">An in-progress Unity project combining game design, API integration, and Azure services.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Current Active Project</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Versus With Verses</strong> is my active game project. It blends my original specialty in Unity game design with the backend and cloud engineering skills I use professionally: API utilization, service boundaries, Azure deployment, and configuration-aware infrastructure.
		</p>
		<p>
			The project is still in progress, so I am presenting it as active development rather than a finished product. The direction is to make a Unity experience that can rely on external content and cloud-backed services without turning the game code into a tangle of direct platform assumptions.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Technical Blend</h2>
		<div class="project-grid">
			<article>
				<h3>Unity Game Design</h3>
				<p>Gameplay flow, interaction design, C# implementation, scene structure, and player-facing iteration.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>API-Driven Content</h3>
				<p>The companion Bible API work supports passage retrieval, translation metadata, recommended versions, and normalized responses.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Azure Services</h3>
				<p>The API is designed for Azure Container Apps, ACR-based image builds, secret-backed app keys, and cloud log inspection.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Separation of Concerns</h3>
				<p>The Unity client can consume purpose-built endpoints instead of directly owning external provider details.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Why It Matters</h2>
		<p>
			This project is a good representation of where my work is heading: creative game systems supported by real backend services. It connects the game-development degree, Unity practice, API design, and Azure operations into one coherent project.
		</p>
	</section>
</div>
